@*
    The Settings page's "Reset all to defaults" control, in the header area. Guarded the way
    Teammates.razor guards Remove: an inline confirm step that swaps the button for Confirm/Cancel in
    place, never a dialog and never a JS confirm() - discarding every customisation in one click with
    no confirmation would be the single most destructive thing this page can do.

    The parent (Settings.razor) owns all state, the same split HooksPanel uses: Confirming and
    AnyModified are both parameters rather than fields here, so the confirm step can be rendered
    directly from a test via ParameterView.FromDictionary, exactly how TeammateCardTests renders
    TeammateCard's ConfirmingRemove state - HtmlRenderer cannot dispatch a click, so there is no other
    way to see this component's confirm step from a test. Every parameter is deliberately non-string
    (two bools, three plain EventCallbacks with no payload) for the same reason HooksPanel's are.
*@

@if (this.Confirming)
{
    <button type="button" class="teammate-card-action teammates-danger" @onclick="this.OnConfirm">Yes, reset everything</button>
    <button type="button" class="teammate-card-action" @onclick="this.OnCancel">Cancel</button>
}
else
{
    <button type="button" class="teammate-card-action teammates-danger" disabled="@(!this.AnyModified)" @onclick="this.OnBeginReset">Reset all to defaults</button>
}

@code {
    /// <summary>Whether any hook currently differs from its catalog default - this drives whether the plain (non-confirming) button is enabled.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool AnyModified { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the inline confirm step is currently showing, in place of the plain button.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Confirming { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when the plain button is clicked, asking the parent to show the confirm step.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnBeginReset { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when the confirm step's "Yes, reset everything" is clicked.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnConfirm { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised when the confirm step's Cancel is clicked, abandoning the reset.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnCancel { get; set; }
}
